Important conditions on reuse, which are part of the attribution requirement
rather than additional licence terms:

1. Offer text in this dataset is quoted from third-party issuers. Reusing a
   quote does not transfer any right in it, and each offer remains subject to
   the issuer's own terms, availability and expiry.
2. The verification date travels with the data. An offer verified on one date
   is not verified on another; always carry `verification.verified_at` and the
   per-source `accessed` dates forward into any reuse.
3. Entries in `data/entries/10-excluded-unverified.json` and the policy notes
   in `data/entries/11-policy-notes.json` document claims that were REJECTED.
   Reusing them as if they were available offers misrepresents the dataset.
4. Flags are part of the record. Removing `flags` while keeping `offer_text`
   strips the caveats the verification produced.
